{
  "source": "Matrix from the CarPlay Developer Guide in the CarKit.Maui specification (2026-10-29). Verify against the latest release before Stage 2. maxActions and defaultLimits are default values to be verified in Stage 3; at runtime the platform limits override them. items: list row kinds (Conversation = CPMessageListItem, iOS 14) and the categories in which they are allowed (Stage 6). Stage 7: the Parking/EvCharging/Fueling, QuickFoodOrdering and DrivingTask category rows are pinned by the spec matrix test; VoiceConversational (iOS 26.4) and PublicSafety/Video are still verified=false (the guide PDF is unreachable), the depth of 3 for conversational categories is confirmed by the guide overview from 2026-02-09; PointsOfInterest 12 without a runtime API. Stage 9: features = platform features with a minimum version (CarFeature; gate with the host asset), VoiceControl maxActions = state action buttons (CPVoiceControlState, iOS 26.4, up to two — WWDC26). Stage 10: category alertActions = CPAlertTemplate.maximumActionCount with the category entitlement (iOS 26.0 probe: audio 1, others 3), the default when there is no runtime limit.",
